{"authored" [{"question" "q-143078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The intensity $I$ of a light source with a motion sensor increases at a rate that's inversely proportional to the square of the distance $d$ from the source to the object detected by the sensor. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the intensity of the light source $I?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **intensity** $I$ of a light source with a motion sensor **increases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **square of the distance** $d$ from the source to the object detected by the sensor.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *intensity* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *square of the distance.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{{d}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the intensity *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{d}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143078" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6c2c5ea9b5746e6ed1772dac175dd03c8a7b8c460ec0c5f94330f3374a220fd0" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{d}^{2}},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basis" 885 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143078" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\text{d}I}{\\text{d}t}=-k{I}^{2},\\,k>0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981296/state.json" "file_sha256" "7921767fdcfd78d2a876f7d806077e36fb55cc7ceb66275ddc01ee0cdadfe93f" "basi