on/worked-solution" "value" "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*In a controlled environment, the **temperature** $T$ of a food container **decreases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **square of the temperature.** *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *temperature $T$* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *square of the temperature $T.$* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{{T}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the temperature *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}T}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{k}{{T}^{2}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/state.json" "file_sha256" "90bad2fcf0b06c97fa465ee12bffb3d9521ecc477ae2496cd63b364d32bf513a" "basis" 1626 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "549df99f0de94e492e4cbdfcb7dd3cdc481fecd08d9c44a86d06fbbf6f4eaf95" "basis" 1626 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14043368/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-143077" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/ho